1. Develop an inventory manager script that stores item names as keys and their current stock



counts as values. The system should update the stock count when a sale occurs and print a

warning if stock drops to zero.




# Inventory Manager

# Store item names and stock counts
inventory = {
    "Pen": 10,
    "Notebook": 5,
    "Pencil": 8
}

# Take sale details
item = input("Enter item sold: ")
quantity = int(input("Enter quantity sold: "))

# Update stock
if item in inventory:
    if quantity <= inventory[item]:
        inventory[item] -= quantity
        print("Sale completed.")
        print("Remaining stock:", inventory[item])

        # Warning if stock becomes zero
        if inventory[item] == 0:
            print("WARNING: Stock is zero!")
    else:
        print("Not enough stock available.")
else:
    print("Item not found.")

# Display inventory
print("\nCurrent Inventory:")
print(inventory)
